// spec: LEX-024, LEX-025, RT-008
//
// ⚠️ A defect is a statement about the INTERPRETER and is never compiled.
//
// LEX-025 makes a Char a Unicode code point -- 0 to 10FFFF, excluding the
// surrogates -- so #233 is e-acute and this must print it.  The range is
// 0..127 instead.
//
// ⚠️ HALF OF THIS DEFECT IS FIXED.  It used to arrive as an uncaught raise
// with no line and no caret, because ScanChar built the value by calling the
// Char built-in, which raises.  It is a scan error and is now reported as one
// [ERR-004].  Only the RANGE remains, and it moves with DEF-01 -- widening a
// Char is the same change as a String of characters rather than bytes.

WriteLn (#233);
